# 🛍️ Olist Customer Satisfaction Dashboard

**PORA Academy · Cohort 7 · Data Analysis · Group 1 Capstone**

A decision-first Streamlit dashboard built on **99,441 Olist orders (2016–2018)** to identify what truly drives customer satisfaction.

> **Primary finding:** Delivery punctuality is the **#1 satisfaction lever**. Late deliveries cost an average of **1.73★** (a **40.2% drop** compared with on-time orders) — a gap that dwarfs any geographic or product-category difference.

🔗 **Live app:** [pora-customer-satisfaction-dashboard](https://pora-customer-satisfaction-dashboard-wu3ymdqefkytau38tt7mss.streamlit.app/)

---

## 📖 Project Overview

While e-commerce businesses often obsess over raw speed, this analysis proves that **reliability** — meeting the promised delivery date — is what actually drives customer loyalty. The dashboard guides stakeholders from high-level KPIs down to statistically verified root causes, ending with prioritized, high-ROI recommendations.

### ✨ Key Features

- **Decision-first navigation:** In-page horizontal tabs (Overview → Customer Satisfaction → Detail & Method → Recommendations) that tell a coherent story.
- **Interactive global filters:** Year and State selectors that dynamically update **every KPI and chart** on the dashboard.
- **Dose–response analysis:** Visualises how satisfaction collapses as delays grow (On Time → Slightly Late → Moderately Late → Severely Late).
- **Statistical rigor:** Welch's t-test, Cohen's *d*, and 95% confidence intervals prove the robustness of the delivery gap.
- **What-if simulator:** An interactive slider projecting the expected average review score if a percentage of late orders were converted to on-time.
- **Geographic insights:** A custom-rendered map of Brazil highlighting review concentration and lagging states (e.g., Rio de Janeiro, Bahia).

---

## 📊 What responds to the filters

The sidebar **Reporting Year** and **State** selectors apply to **every KPI and chart** on the dashboard. Set both filters to **All** to reproduce the reference numbers.

| Element | Filtered? |
|---|---|
| Executive summary + headline strip | ✅ Yes |
| KPI row (orders, delivered, avg review, late, avg delivery days) | ✅ Yes |
| **Review score distribution** | ✅ **Yes** |
| Monthly average review score | ✅ Yes |
| Average review score by state (top 10) | ✅ Yes |
| On-time vs late by state (top 5) | ✅ Yes |
| Delivery punctuality vs satisfaction (+ what-if) | ✅ Yes |
| Satisfaction by delivery-time bucket (reference line = selection average) | ✅ Yes |
| Brazil map (selected states coloured, others greyed; year filtered) | ✅ Yes |
| "Insight" line under every chart | ✅ Yes — recomputed from the selection |
| Detail & Method diagnostic tables | ❌ No — whole-dataset data-quality checks |
| Recommendations tab | ❌ No — decisions are based on the whole dataset |

All filtered queries share one definition (`apply_filters()` in `olist_app.py`), so every chart filters identically.

